---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import StatusBadge from '../components/StatusBadge.astro';
import { STATUS_META } from '../data/types';
import { CONTACT } from '../data/site';

const statuses = (
  ['confirmed', 'supplied', 'estimate', 'assumption', 'in-progress', 'outstanding'] as const
).map((key) => ({ key, ...STATUS_META[key] }));
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Information Accuracy"
  description="How Yala Energy labels factual claims, estimates and assumptions on this website, and the limits of the information published here."
  path="/information-accuracy/"
  lede="Development-stage projects are built on a mix of documented fact, company information, estimates and assumptions. This page explains how we distinguish them, and what the information on this site can and cannot be used for."
  updated="27 October 2026"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Why this page exists</h2>
    <p>
      It is ordinary for a project website to present capacity, cost and yield figures as though
      they were all equally settled. They never are. At early development stage, some numbers come
      from documents, some from the company's own records, some from estimates and some from
      working assumptions that will change.
    </p>
    <p>
      Presenting them as one undifferentiated set of facts is how due diligence becomes expensive
      and how trust gets lost. So every substantive claim on this site carries a status, and this
      page says what each status means.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The labels</h2>
    <dl class="accuracy-list">
      {
        statuses.map((item) => (
          <div class="accuracy-list__row">
            <dt><StatusBadge status={item.key} explain={false} /></dt>
            <dd>{item.description}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is not claimed anywhere on this site</h2>
    <p>
      As at the last review of this content, the Muchenje Solar PV Plant does not have, and this
      website does not claim it has:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A signed power purchase agreement, or an agreed tariff.</li>
      <li>A generation licence or any other energy-sector authorisation.</li>
      <li>Environmental or social approval, or a completed impact assessment.</li>
      <li>A grid-connection agreement, or confirmed network capacity.</li>
      <li>Financial close, committed debt, or a committed equity investor.</li>
      <li>Bankability certification, or completed lender technical due diligence.</li>
      <li>Procured equipment, or a contracted EPC provider.</li>
      <li>A site-specific, independently reviewed energy-yield assessment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The terms "shovel-ready" and "bankable" are not used of this project, because neither would
      be accurate today.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Endorsements</h2>
    <p>
      No organisation named on this website endorses Yala Energy Limited or its projects. In
      particular:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        References to ZESCO describe the network operator the project intends to connect to. There
        is no agreement, arrangement or endorsement, and no approval has been granted.
      </li>
      <li>
        References to RatedPower and Enverus describe software we use under licence. They do not
        imply ownership, partnership, reseller status, certification or endorsement.
      </li>
      <li>
        Organisations named in the leadership biographies are previous or current affiliations of
        the individual concerned. They say nothing about Yala Energy.
      </li>
      <li>
        References to World Bank Group, ESMAP and Solargis solar-resource mapping describe a public
        data source used for preliminary screening only.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Technical figures</h2>
    <p>
      Capacities, yields, line lengths, land areas and costs shown on this site are design
      assumptions or estimates at concept stage unless they carry the "confirmed" label. They will
      change as feasibility work, grid studies and equipment selection progress, and they are not
      warranted as accurate, complete or current.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a storage figure is given in MWh it is an energy capacity, not a power rating in MW.
      Where a generation figure is given in MWp it is peak DC capacity, not AC export capacity.
      The two are routinely confused and we try hard not to add to it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Not an offer, and not advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this website is an offer to sell, or a solicitation of an offer to buy, any
      security or interest in any project or company. Nothing here is investment, legal,
      engineering or tax advice, and nothing here should be relied on as the basis of an investment
      or engineering decision.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any investment or partnership would follow mutual due diligence, independent verification
      and documented commercial terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Consulting outputs</h2>
    <p>
      The PV and BESS engineering services described on this site are preliminary and
      feasibility-level unless a specific engagement scope says otherwise. They do not replace
      detailed design, protection studies, grid-code compliance work, manufacturer validation or
      the sign-off of a licensed design authority. Financial outputs are scenarios, not forecasts
      or guarantees.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Imagery</h2>
    <p>
      Photographs on this site that are not of the Muchenje site are captioned as illustrative and
      explicitly identified as not being the Muchenje site. Where no photograph is available, the
      artwork is original illustration and is identified as such. No image on this site is
      presented as a photograph of a built Yala Energy asset, because there is not yet one to
      photograph.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tell us if something is wrong</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe anything on this site is inaccurate, out of date or misleading, email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>. We would rather correct it than
      defend it.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalLayout>

<style>
  .accuracy-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .accuracy-list__row {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    padding-block-end: var(--space-md);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .accuracy-list__row {
      grid-template-columns: 11rem minmax(0, 1fr);
      align-items: baseline;
    }
  }
</style>
